,"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":237,"path":238,"stem":239,"icon":174},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":241,"path":242,"stem":243,"icon":33},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":245,"path":246,"stem":247,"icon":248},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":250,"path":251,"stem":252,"icon":253},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":255,"path":256,"stem":257,"icon":258},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":260,"title":171,"body":261,"description":585,"extension":586,"links":587,"meta":588,"navigation":589,"path":172,"seo":590,"stem":173,"__hash__":591},"docs\u002F04.platform\u002F01.architecture.md",{"type":262,"value":263,"toc":576},"minimark",[264,268,272,276,340,348,352,420,424,427,437,443,448,459,504,510,514,536,569,572],[265,266,26],"h2",{"id":267},"overview",[269,270,271],"p",{},"Kinotic OS is a full-stack application platform that handles service communication, persistence, authentication, authorization, deployment, and observability. The system is composed of several core components that work together to provide a seamless development and runtime experience.",[265,273,275],{"id":274},"core-components","Core Components",[277,278,279,296,309,322,328,334],"ul",{},[280,281,282,286,287,291,292,295],"li",{},[283,284,285],"strong",{},"Management server"," (",[288,289,290],"code",{},"kinotic-server-management",") — The API the portal, the Kinotic CLI and organization members' MCP hosts call: sign-up, logins and invitations, the ",[288,293,294],{},"management-api"," services, and the GitHub App's webhook.",[280,297,298,286,301,304,305,308],{},[283,299,300],{},"System server",[288,302,303],{},"kinotic-server-system",") — The API the system console and the vm-managers call: the ",[288,306,307],{},"system-api"," services, project deployments, and the cluster singletons that reconcile deployments and delete old workload runs.",[280,310,311,286,314,317,318,321],{},[283,312,313],{},"App server",[288,315,316],{},"kinotic-server-app",") — The API every application's users, UIs and microservices call: the ",[288,319,320],{},"app-api"," persistence services and the services applications publish in their own zones, each application at its own API host.",[280,323,324,327],{},[283,325,326],{},"RPC Gateway"," — Each server's gateway routes remote procedure calls between its clients and published services over STOMP\u002FWebSocket, and serves the server's REST and MCP endpoints.",[280,329,330,333],{},[283,331,332],{},"Persistence Layer"," — Provides automatic CRUD operations for entities backed by Elasticsearch.",[280,335,336,339],{},[283,337,338],{},"Auth System"," — Handles authentication (email\u002Fpassword and OIDC) across three authorization hierarchies: System, Organization, and Application. Each server admits only the participants it serves.",[269,341,342,343,347],{},"The three servers are Spring Boot applications that form one Ignite cluster, in which each hosts only its own zones. ",[344,345,194],"a",{"href":346},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fdefense-in-depth#network-architecture"," shows which participants each admits and which zones each hosts.",[265,349,351],{"id":350},"tech-stack","Tech Stack",[353,354,355,368],"table",{},[356,357,358],"thead",{},[359,360,361,365],"tr",{},[362,363,364],"th",{},"Component",[362,366,367],{},"Technology",[369,370,371,380,388,396,404,412],"tbody",{},[359,372,373,377],{},[374,375,376],"td",{},"Orchestration",[374,378,379],{},"Kubernetes",[359,381,382,385],{},[374,383,384],{},"Build Isolation",[374,386,387],{},"Firecracker VMs",[359,389,390,393],{},[374,391,392],{},"Runtime",[374,394,395],{},"Bun",[359,397,398,401],{},[374,399,400],{},"Search\u002FPersistence",[374,402,403],{},"Elasticsearch",[359,405,406,409],{},[374,407,408],{},"Logging",[374,410,411],{},"Grafana Loki",[359,413,414,417],{},[374,415,416],{},"Payments",[374,418,419],{},"Stripe Connect",[265,421,423],{"id":422},"communication","Communication",[269,425,426],{},"Services communicate via STOMP over WebSocket, with messages routed by CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier). Each service, method, and event stream is addressable through a CRI, which follows the format:",[428,429,434],"pre",{"className":430,"code":432,"language":433},[431],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[288,435,432],{"__ignoreMap":436},"",[269,438,439,440,442],{},"The RPC gateway uses CRIs to route requests to the correct service instance, apply versioning, and enforce scope-based multi-tenancy. See the ",[344,441,227],{"href":228}," reference for details.",[444,445,447],"h3",{"id":446},"kinotic-rpc-on-its-own","Kinotic RPC on its own",[269,449,450,451,454,455,458],{},"Kinotic RPC, the service and event layer in ",[288,452,453],{},"kinotic-core"," and ",[288,456,457],{},"kinotic-api-gateway",", runs without the rest of\nKinotic OS. A server built on it alone supplies two beans the gateway authenticates and authorizes every\nconnection with:",[353,460,461,471],{},[356,462,463],{},[359,464,465,468],{},[362,466,467],{},"Bean",[362,469,470],{},"What it decides",[369,472,473,486],{},[359,474,475,480],{},[374,476,477],{},[288,478,479],{},"SecurityService",[374,481,482,483],{},"Who a connection is: it authenticates the STOMP CONNECT headers and returns the connection's ",[288,484,485],{},"Participant",[359,487,488,493],{},[374,489,490],{},[288,491,492],{},"ZoneRulesResolver",[374,494,495,496,499,500,503],{},"What that participant may address: the ",[288,497,498],{},"ZoneRules"," of zones it may send to and subscribe in, which the gateway narrows to the zones the server's ",[288,501,502],{},"ZonePartitioningService"," serves",[269,505,506,507,509],{},"Kinotic OS's servers supply each from their own module: the ",[288,508,479],{}," of the server, and kinotic-domain's\nresolver, which gives system, organization and application participants their zones.",[444,511,513],{"id":512},"never-block-the-event-loop","Never block the event loop",[269,515,516,517,520,521,524,525,524,528,531,532,535],{},"A Java service published with ",[288,518,519],{},"@Publish"," is invoked on a Vert.x event loop it shares with the other services on the node, the same rule Vert.x sets for its own handlers. A method returns a ",[288,522,523],{},"Future",", ",[288,526,527],{},"CompletableFuture",[288,529,530],{},"Mono"," or ",[288,533,534],{},"Flux"," and lets the work complete off the loop; a method that is slow, because it blocks on a synchronous client, a lock or a sleep, or because it does heavy CPU work, hands that work off inside itself:",[428,537,541],{"className":538,"code":539,"language":540,"meta":436,"style":436},"language-java shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","@Override\npublic Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n}\n","java",[288,542,543,551,557,563],{"__ignoreMap":436},[544,545,548],"span",{"class":546,"line":547},"line",1,[544,549,550],{},"@Override\n",[544,552,554],{"class":546,"line":553},2,[544,555,556],{},"public Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n",[544,558,560],{"class":546,"line":559},3,[544,561,562],{},"    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n",[544,564,566],{"class":546,"line":565},4,[544,567,568],{},"}\n",[269,570,571],{},"The platform never hands off on a service's behalf. A method that blocks stalls every service sharing its loop, and Vert.x's blocked-thread checker reports it in the log.",[573,574,575],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":436,"searchDepth":553,"depth":553,"links":577},[578,579,580,581],{"id":267,"depth":553,"text":26},{"id":274,"depth":553,"text":275},{"id":350,"depth":553,"text":351},{"id":422,"depth":553,"text":423,"children":582},[583,584],{"id":446,"depth":559,"text":447},{"id":512,"depth":559,"text":513},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.","md",null,{},{"icon":174},{"title":171,"description":585},"ggXFHW1jM4SzoVJQNjkBWucJSO-WTGMjCfB23F0MG90",[593,595],{"title":162,"path":163,"stem":164,"description":594,"icon":85,"children":-1},"Complete SQL grammar reference for migration scripts.",{"title":176,"path":177,"stem":178,"description":596,"icon":6,"children":-1},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.",1793101245654]